The '''Republic of Meridiana''' ({{Langx|ca|República de Meridiana}}) was a [[W:Buffer state|buffer state]] in [[Estuaria]] (southern [[Balisca]]) that acted as a [[W:Puppet state|puppet state]] of [[Potocsí]]. On 18 November 1918, Potocsino military forces invaded southern Balisca as part of a larger [[Foreign intervention in the Baliscan Revolution|foreign intervention]] during the [[Baliscan Revolution]], in an attempt to prop up the [[Nationalists (Baliscan Revolution)|Nationalist]] government of [[Máximo Burjassot]]. The state came to an end when it was re-annexed into [[Balisca]] at the start of the [[Abyalan Campaign]] of the [[Great Adonian War]]. 

On 20 January 1919, the Potocsino military announced its intention to [[Potocsino occupation of Quiscosta|annex the territory of Quiscosta]], sparking outrage amongst many Nationalist leaders and local communities. While vocally opposing the annexation, Nationalist forces assisted Potocsino forces in [[1919 massacres in Quiscosta|violently suppressing the local protests]], in fear of them being revolutionary-aligned. Discussions between the Nationalists and the Potocsino occupation forces would result in the formation of the Republic of Meridiana, consisting of the Potocsino-occupied territories in Southern Balisca. 

Though Meridiana garnered no international recognition, it was propped up by neighboring [[Potocsí]]. Despite this support, the authority of the Republic rapidly deteriorated as clashes between it and Baliscan forces intensified. The [[Confederal Armed Forces|Baliscan Armed Forces]] launched a [[W:Blitzkrieg|lightning offensive]] against the territory in 193x, rapidly overwhelming its defenses and liberating the entirety of the territory within days.

